# `SELECT *` after a pipe: `project *` is not valid, so the fix is not certain.
mode: syntax
---- query
from t | SELECT *
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..18
  PIPELINE@0..17
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    ERROR@9..17
      IDENT@9..15 "SELECT"
      WHITESPACE@15..16 " "
      STAR@16..17 "*"
  WHITESPACE@17..18 "\n"

error[DS0105]: SQL keyword `SELECT` is not an operator
  --> query:1:10
  |
1 | from t | SELECT *
  |          ^^^^^^ this is SQL
  |
  = help: every column is kept already: remove `| SELECT *`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from t
which parses without errors
